package "pkg/fvanon"

// Field takes a source-level ANONYMOUS struct (struct{ x int }, SizeOf 4 on ILP32)
// BY VALUE and returns its field.  A source-level anon struct is COERCED: IR-gen
// names it `__anon_N`, so AggInRegCoercedKind — and AggCoercedInReg — is TRUE, and
// isByAddressAggArm32 is TRUE via branch 1 (the same as a named struct).  Under
// `-backend native` this package is LLVM-compiled, so native `main` forming a
// *func(struct{ x int }) int = Field and calling it exercises the cross-mode
// marshaling for the coerced shape: native `emitCallFuncValue` passes the anon struct
// BY-ADDRESS as one dispatch pointer word, main's own native marshaling shim
// re-expands it into the coerced slot, and it tail-branches to this LLVM-compiled
// `Field`, which reads its coerced param.  (The LLVM shim for Field — a distinct weak
// @__shim.<Field> that main never calls — likewise declares the coerced arg i8*.)
func Field(s struct { x int }) int
